Hello,

On my laptop, plugging in or unplugging the AC adapter causes a complete
system freeze (frozen screen, no input, requiring a hard power-off). Resume
from suspend also became very slow. This started right after upgrading from
kernel 7.2.10 to 7.2.11. After downgrading back to 7.2.10, the problem is
gone with ~6 days of normal use with no freezes and no SMU errors in the
kernel log.

My Hardware:

   - Laptop: Lenovo Ideapad Slim 5 (14AKP10)
   - BIOS: R0CN27WW (01/09/2026)
   - CPU/GPU: AMD Ryzen AI 7 350 / Radeon 860M (amdgpu at 0000:04:00.0)
   - RAM: 24 GB

Software Information:

   - Distribution: Arch Linux
   - Kernel: 7.2.11-arch1-1 (bad), 7.2.10-arch1-1 (good)
   - linux-firmware: 20260916-1 (same on good and bad kernel)
   - Mesa: 26.2.5
   - Desktop: GNOME (Wayland), power-profiles-daemon 0.30

Steps to reproduce:

   1. Boot 7.2.11
   2. Plug in or unplug the AC adapter
   3. System freezes within seconds

Occurrence: most times I plug or unplug the charger.

Log from the frozen boot:

amdgpu 0000:04:00.0: SMU: No response msg_reg: f resp_reg: 0
in params:00000007
ucsi_acpi USBC000:00: ucsi_handle_connector_change: GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS
failed (-110)
ACPI Error: Aborting method _SB.A018 due to previous error
(AE_AML_LOOP_TIMEOUT)
ACPI Error: Aborting method _SB.ALIB due to previous error
(AE_AML_LOOP_TIMEOUT)
ACPI Error: Aborting method _SB.ACAD._PSR due to previous error
(AE_AML_LOOP_TIMEOUT)
ACPI Error: Aborting method _SB.PCI0.LPC0.EC0.VPC0.GBMD due to previous
error (AE_AML_LOOP_TIMEOUT)

The SMU message repeats every ~5 seconds until power-off. The first
occurrence in my journal is 2026-10-19, the day after the 7.2.11 upgrade;
no earlier boot has these errors.

Full kernel log and amdgpu_firmware_info are attached. I'm happy to test
patches or bisect between 7.2.10 and 7.2.11 if that helps.

Thanks,
Ashaz Qureshi

